{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792352430,"nonce":"cMf8j64LwAcVfd0uSsLKr9smO38=","title":"ash serve ignores HTTP Range requests and sends media files as octet-stream","message":"A page's \u003caudio\u003e element cannot seek a file served by ash serve: a Range request is answered 200 with the whole body, there is no Accept-Ranges, and an .m4a goes out as application/octet-stream (ashui, 2026-10-18; their page now fetches the file whole when the server offers no ranges). Answer a single bytes=a-b, a-, or -n range with 206, Content-Range and Accept-Ranges, 416 for one past the end, and give audio and video files their media types.","files":null}]}